# Maximal error of functions.
#
# Measured maximum, not a margin.  On this tree (2026-11-24, qemu 11.0.0,
# RVV 1.0) the default rounding mode reaches 1 ULP for all 60 variants on the
# upstream libm-test corpus, and for the 25 fixed-length variants measured
# with a 1M-input-per-function random corpus (5 functions x m1/m2/m4/m8 at
# VLEN=128, plus m8 at VLEN=512; no VLA and no masked variants).  Read the
# per-block value from the driver's -v -v output: the final "Maximum error
# found" line reflects the last summary block, which is empty for vector
# tests.
#
# Vector tests only execute the default rounding mode: math/libm-test-driver.c
# guards the directed-rounding input loops with !TEST_MATHVEC, so the three
# extra summary blocks are printed without running any cases and carry no
# accuracy result.  This file therefore only gates the default (RNE) test
# name, e.g. log_rvv_m2.
#
# The scalar dbl-64 log documents worst-case 0.507 ULP near 1 and 0.519 ULP
# elsewhere; that is background for the ported algorithm, not a proven bound
# for the vector kernels.  The integer gate above records the measured
# encoding-step maximum; an entry still matters because without one the
# driver accepts up to 9 ULP, and a key that matches no test name is
# silently ignored.  Re-measure after kernel changes.

